51 [Rev. January 1, 2007]\n\nNOTICE OF MOTION AND MOTION  \nTO BE RELIEVED AS COUNSEL—CIVIL\n\nCode of Civil Procedure, § 284;  \nCal. Rules of Court, rule 3.1362  \nwww.courtinfo.ca.gov--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMC–051\nATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY (Name, s (https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/mc051.pdf)\nciteturn1691search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; MC–051 ... www.courtinfo.ca.gov\nMC–051\nATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY (Name, slate bar number, and address):\nTELEPHONE NO.: FAX NO.:\nATTORNEY FOR (Name):  | FOR COURT USE ONLY\nTo keep other people from\nseeing what you entered on\nyour form, please press the\nClear This Form button at the\nend of the form when finished.\n--- | ---\nNAME OF COURT:\nSTREET ADDRESS:\nMAILING ADDRESS:\nCITY AND ZIP CODE:\nBRANCH NAME:  | \nCASE NAME:  | CASE NUMBER:\nNOTICE OF MOTION AND MOTION\nTO BE RELIEVED AS\nCOUNSEL—CIVIL  | HEARING DATE:\nDEPT.: TIME:\nBEFORE HON.:\nDATE ACTION FILED:\nTRIAL DATE:TO (name and address of client):\n1.   PLEASE TAKE NOTICE that (name of withdrawing attorney):\nmoves under California Code of Civil Procedure section 284(2) and California Rules of Court, rule 3.1362, for an order permitting \nthe attorney to be relieved as attorney of record in this action or proceeding.\n2.   A hearing on this motion to be relieved as counsel will be held as follows:\nDate:\na.\nTime:\nDept.:\nRoom:\nb.  The address of the court:\nother (specify):\nsame as noted above\n3.   This motion is supported by the accompanying declaration, the papers and records filed in this action or proceeding, and\n      the following additional documents or evidence (specify):\n(This motion does not need to be accompanied by a memorandum of points and authorities. Cal. Rules of Court, rule 3.1362.)\n4.   The client presently represented by the attorney is\na.\na trustee.\nan individual.\ng.\nh.\nb.\na personal representative.\na corporation.\na probate fiduciary.\na partnership.\ni.\nc.\na guardian ad litem.\nd.\nj.\nan unincorporated association.\nk.\ne.\nother (specify):\na guardian.\nf.\na conservator.\n(Continued on reverse)\nPage 1 of 2\nForm Adopted for Mandatory Use \nJudicial Council of California \nMC-051 [Rev. January 1, 2007]\nCode of Civil Procedure , § 284; \nCal. Rules of Court, rule 3.1362\nwww.courtinfo.ca.gov\nNOTICE OF MOTION AND MOTION \nTO BE RELIEVED AS COUNSEL—CIVIL--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNotice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/MC-051)\nciteturn1691search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil (MC-051)Attorneys use this to ask the court to let them stop representing a client in a civil case.\n\n# Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil (MC-051)\n\nAttorneys use this to ask the court to let them stop representing a client in a civil case. Also provides information to clients who will no longer be represented by an attorney.\n\nGet form MC-051\n\nEffective: January 1, 2007--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSP09-03 \nInvitation to Comment \n | SP09-03 Invitat (https://www.courts.ca.gov/partners/documents/comment.pdf)\nciteturn1691search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; MC–051 ... but you may NOT proceed without an attorney in most other court matters, including some matters governed by that code.\nMC–051\nCASE NAME:\nCASE NUMBER:\nNOTICE TO CERTAIN CLIENTS CONCERNING LEGAL REPRESENTATION\nIf this motion to be relieved as counsel is granted, your present attorney will no longer be representing you. If you are one \nof the parties listed below, YOU SHOULD IMMEDIATELY SEEK LEGAL ADVICE REGARDING LEGAL REPRESENTATION. \nFailure to retain an attorney may lead to an order striking your pleadings or to the entry of a default judgment against you.\nIf you are a guardian ad litem, a corporation, or an unincorporated association, you may NOT act as your own attorney in \nmost cases. \n•\n•\nIf you are an attorney-in-fact, a guardian of a minor, a conservator, a personal representative of a decedent's estate \n(executor or administrator), or a trustee, you may act as your own attorney in most matters governed by the Probate Code, \nbut you may NOT proceed without an attorney in most other court matters, including some matters governed by that code. See \nrule 7.15 of the California Rules of Court. \n5.  If this motion is granted and a client is representing himself or herself, the client will be solely responsible for the case.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=1&query=civil)\nciteturn1691search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009 ...   * MC-051 * Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil Effective: January 1, 2007\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-012 * Memorandum of Costs After Judgment, Acknowledgement of Credit, and Declaration of Accrued Interest Effective: January 1, 2026\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-013-INFO Information Sheet for Calculating Interest and Amount Owed on a Judgment Effective: January 1, 2026\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-051 * Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil Effective: January 1, 2007\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-052 * Declaration in Support of Attorney's Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil Effective: January 1, 2007\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-053 * Order Granting Attorney's Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil Effective: January 1, 2007\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-125 * Confidential Information Form Under Civil Code Section 1708.85 or 1708.89 Effective: January 1, 2026\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * POS-015 * Notice and Acknowledgment of Receipt—Civil Effective: January 1, 2005\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * POS-020 Proof of Personal Service—Civil (Proof of Service) / Information Sheet for Proof of Personal Service—Civil Effective: January 1, 2005\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * POS-020(D) Attachment to Proof of Personal Service—Civil (Documents Served) Effective: January 1, 2005\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=1&query=SC-)\nciteturn1691search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009 ...   * MC-051 * Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil Effective: January 1, 2007\n\n# Find Your Court Forms\n\nSearch for any topic or form number, view all forms or view all forms by category\n\nFulltext search [Input]\n\n[Input]\n\nwarning alert banner:\n\n### Don't fill forms in your browser!\n\nUse Adobe Reader. See instructions.\n\nFound 315 forms matching \"SC-\".\n\nForms marked with the asterisk (\"*\") are adopted for mandatory use by all courts.\n\n  * MC-011 Memorandum of Costs (Worksheet) Effective: January 1, 2025\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-012 * Memorandum of Costs After Judgment, Acknowledgement of Credit, and Declaration of Accrued Interest Effective: January 1, 2026\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-013-INFO Information Sheet for Calculating Interest and Amount Owed on a Judgment Effective: January 1, 2026\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-020 Additional Page [to be attached to any form] Effective: January 1, 1987\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-025 Attachment to Judicial Council Form Effective: July 1, 2009 español\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-030 Declaration Effective: January 1, 2006\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-031 Attached Declaration Effective: July 1, 2005\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-040 Notice of Change of Address or Other Contact Effective: January 1, 2013\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * MC-051 * Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil Effective: January 1, 2007\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRule 3.1362. Motion to be relieved as counsel | Judicial Branch of California (https://courts.ca.gov/cms/rules/index/three/rule3_1362)\nciteturn1691search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; A notice of motion and motion to be relieved as counsel under Code of Civil Procedure section 284(2) must be directed to the client and must be made on the Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel-Civil (form MC-051). ... The proposed order relieving counsel must be prepared on the Order Granting Attorney's Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel-Civil (form MC-053) and must be lodged with the court with the moving papers.\n\nCalifornia Rules of Court 2026\n\n# Rule 3.1362. Motion to be relieved as counsel\n\n(a) Notice\n\nA notice of motion and motion to be relieved as counsel under Code of Civil Procedure section 284(2) must be directed to the client and must be made on the Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel-Civil (form MC-051).\n\n(Subd (a) amended effective January 1, 2007; previously amended effective July 1, 2000.)\n\n(b) Memorandum\n\nNotwithstanding any other rule of court, no memorandum is required to be filed or served with a motion to be relieved as counsel.\n\n(Subd (b) amended effective January 1, 2007; adopted effective July 1, 2000.)\n\n(c) Declaration\n\nThe motion to be relieved as counsel must be accompanied by a declaration on the Declaration in Support of Attorney's Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel-Civil (form MC-052). The declaration must state in general terms and without compromising the confidentiality of the attorney-client relationship why a motion under Code of Civil Procedure section 284(2) is brought instead of filing a consent under Code of Civil Procedure section 284(1).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms/all-by-category)\nciteturn1691search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009 ...   * MC-051 * Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil Effective: January 1, 2007\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=10&query=RT-)\nciteturn1691search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009 ...   * MC-051 * Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil Effective: January 1, 2007\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=12&query=TH-)\nciteturn1691search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009 ...   * MC-051 * Notice of Motion and Motion to Be Relieved as Counsel—Civil Effective: January 1, 2007\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=11&query=DE-)\nciteturn1691search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009 ...   * MC-05